## 3.6 Project Management Plan

### 3.6.1 Team Organisation and Responsibilities

The project was executed by a team in which responsibilities were distributed according to individual competencies. Primary areas of responsibility included dataset acquisition and preprocessing, model implementation (LCDNet, MobileCount, CSRNet, routing classifier), training script development, evaluation and benchmarking, and documentation and thesis writing. All team members contributed to code review and integration testing.

Regular weekly meetings were conducted to allocate tasks, monitor progress, address technical issues, and review intermediate deliverables. The project supervisor provided guidance and reviewed progress at scheduled intervals throughout the development cycle.

### 3.6.2 Development Methodology

The project followed an iterative, milestone-driven development methodology structured into four principal phases:

**Phase 1 — Foundation and Data Preparation:** Setup of the development environment, dataset acquisition (NWPU-Crowd, ShanghaiTech), preprocessing pipeline implementation, and initial baseline experiments with LCDNet on the ShanghaiTech dataset.

**Phase 2 — Model Implementation and Individual Training:** Independent training of the routing classifier (MobileNetV2), LCDNet on the NWPU-Crowd sparse subset, and MobileCount on the NWPU-Crowd dense subset using the standard training pipeline.

**Phase 3 — Knowledge Distillation and System Integration:** Implementation of the CSRNet-to-MobileCount knowledge distillation pipeline, integration of all three components into the hybrid inference system, and implementation of both hard-routing and soft-fusion inference modes.

**Phase 4 — Evaluation, Analysis, and Documentation:** Comprehensive evaluation on the NWPU-Crowd validation set and ShanghaiTech cross-dataset benchmarks, threshold sweep analysis, router calibration assessment, failure case analysis, and thesis writing.

### 3.6.3 Version Control and Reproducibility

A Git repository hosted on GitHub was used throughout the project for version control, collaborative development, and issue tracking. All training scripts, configuration files, preprocessing routines, and evaluation scripts are maintained within the repository under a clearly documented directory structure. Checkpoint files are externally stored and linked via the repository's documentation to ensure that results can be fully reproduced. This approach follows established practices for reproducible machine learning research [Pineau et al., 2021].

### 3.6.4 Project Timeline

| Phase | Activities | Duration |
|---|---|---|
| Phase 1 | Environment setup, dataset preparation, baseline experiments | Weeks 1–4 |
| Phase 2 | Routing classifier training, LCDNet fine-tuning, MobileCount training | Weeks 5–9 |
| Phase 3 | Knowledge distillation, system integration, inference pipeline | Weeks 10–13 |
| Phase 4 | Evaluation, analysis, documentation, thesis writing | Weeks 14–18 |

### 3.6.5 Tools and Infrastructure

The project was developed using the following tools and infrastructure:

- **Programming Language:** Python 3.x
- **Deep Learning Framework:** PyTorch 2.x with torchvision
- **Hardware:** NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 (training), NVIDIA Jetson Nano (target deployment platform)
- **Version Control:** Git / GitHub
- **Documentation:** Markdown, LaTeX
- **Computational Analysis:** thop (FLOPs estimation), fvcore, scipy

